        "original_id": "33380e59-842b-526c-b5a8-03f8cb05d09d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cadore, Belluno, Veneto, Austria, Trentino-Alto Adige/Südtirol, Friuli-Venezia Giulia, Dolomite Mountains, Northern Italy, South Tyrol, Trentino, Italy\n- Languages: Ladin, Venetian, German, Sappada German, Friulian, Italian, Rhaeto-Romance\n- Peoples and folklore: Ladin people, Longana\n\nFacts:\n- Cadore is a historical region in Veneto in the northernmost part of the province of Belluno, and it borders Austria, Trentino-Alto Adige/Südtirol, and Friuli-Venezia Giulia.\n- Cadore is also known by names in Ladin, Venetian, German, Sappada German, and Friulian.\n- Ladin is a Romance language made up of a group of dialects, and some consider it part of a unitary Rhaeto-Romance language.\n- Ladin is mainly spoken by the Ladin people in the Dolomite Mountains of Northern Italy, including South Tyrol, Trentino, and the province of Belluno.\n- The Longana are legendary creatures that appear in the legends of people living in Cadore, Italy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
